	<item>
		<title>By: Najat Roberts</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=295&#038;cpage=1#comment-12210</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Najat Roberts]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 03 Jul 2012 22:01:51 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=295#comment-12210</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[We were friends many years.  When in southern California he considered me one of his checkpoints because we could speak on the phone often.  He was leading a fledgling center in San Diego and I was in Torrance then.  We exchanged letters regularly.  We laughed a lot.  We discussed the esoteric lessons.  When my family and I went to San Diego for a vacation, we visited him there and our son Phil was enchanted by this big bear of a man.  We did our best to keep each other shining and listening.  We were enriched by our shared commitment to the work.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>We were friends many years.  When in southern California he considered me one of his checkpoints because we could speak on the phone often.  He was leading a fledgling center in San Diego and I was in Torrance then.  We exchanged letters regularly.  We laughed a lot.  We discussed the esoteric lessons.  When my family and I went to San Diego for a vacation, we visited him there and our son Phil was enchanted by this big bear of a man.  We did our best to keep each other shining and listening.  We were enriched by our shared commitment to the work.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Luccia Jalila</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=295&#038;cpage=1#comment-8152</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Luccia Jalila]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 10 May 2011 07:52:27 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=295#comment-8152</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Teacher of my teacher, grandfather of my heart and soul, lover of Allah ...

I was told to meet him by Khaliq, my teacher and his mureed when I went to graduate school. I learned quickly what seemed to be gruffness masked a heart, &quot;two sizes too large.&quot; He was direct and honest, but would smile and a flood of love would pour outward.

He once went to meet Matthew Fox. He brought his flute and played for him. It was a short meeting, but when I met Matt and mentioned I knew Ahmaddin, he smiled and told of the stranger who sat in his office just to play his flute. He sent his regards and love and I passed those along the best I could.

Ahmaddin trained me as I engaged in graduate work to become a Cheraga. He ordained me after I received my degree saying, &quot;Allah makes one a Cheraga, ordination is our way of recognizing it.&quot;

When I lived in Khankah SAM, I was honored to have Ahmaddin&#039;s guidance and friendship. Even though my life path took me far away, I still can sit quietly, think of him, and the waves of love pour over me again.

His light, his teaching, his love still shine as he was a channel clear and open to the message and love of the Source of All.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Teacher of my teacher, grandfather of my heart and soul, lover of Allah &#8230;</p>
<p>I was told to meet him by Khaliq, my teacher and his mureed when I went to graduate school. I learned quickly what seemed to be gruffness masked a heart, &#8220;two sizes too large.&#8221; He was direct and honest, but would smile and a flood of love would pour outward.</p>
<p>He once went to meet Matthew Fox. He brought his flute and played for him. It was a short meeting, but when I met Matt and mentioned I knew Ahmaddin, he smiled and told of the stranger who sat in his office just to play his flute. He sent his regards and love and I passed those along the best I could.</p>
<p>Ahmaddin trained me as I engaged in graduate work to become a Cheraga. He ordained me after I received my degree saying, &#8220;Allah makes one a Cheraga, ordination is our way of recognizing it.&#8221;</p>
<p>When I lived in Khankah SAM, I was honored to have Ahmaddin&#8217;s guidance and friendship. Even though my life path took me far away, I still can sit quietly, think of him, and the waves of love pour over me again.</p>
<p>His light, his teaching, his love still shine as he was a channel clear and open to the message and love of the Source of All.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
